Philosophy (UIDP) in Punjab, India \n\n Pursue Ph.D. at India’s Leading Research-Intensive University \n\n Research is the cornerstone of the educational paradigm at Chandigarh University. From research-oriented curricula, industry-collaborated centres of excellence, and cutting-edge laboratories, to an extensive network with government organisations, corporates, and international universities, students receive ample opportunities to excel in their research endeavours. \n\n Apply Today for Doctorate Programs \n\n Registration End Date : 23 rd April, 2026 \r\n\n Registration Closed\n\n Already Registered (https://www.cuchd.in/phd-me-admissions/ApplicationLogin.aspx?Subject=fJAt3RX8ggEX//eDGysKyA==) \r\n\n Best University Institute of Doctorate of Philosophy (UIDP) in Punjab, India\n\n A Doctorate of Philosophy (Ph.D.) is a research-based doctorate program that offers core specialization in a certain domain. A Ph.D. can be obtained in most academic areas and provides specific education in a discipline, followed by postdoctoral on-the-job training. An eligible academic authority supervises the research undertaken during the program. It is a degree awarded for research, which exhibits the competence of an individual to conduct independent research, contributing to the knowledge of the subject.\n\n Explore More \r\n\n Leading in an Impact-Driven \n Research Ecosystem\n\n 0 \r\n PUBLICATIONS\n\n Scopus-Indexed\nPublications\n\n 0 \r\n PATENTS\n\n Filed in\nDiverse Domains\n\n 0 \r\n CITATIONS\n\n Scopus\nCitations\n\n 0 \r\n IMPACT\n\n H-Index\n\n 0 \r\n CRORES+\n\n Government Funded\nResearch Projects\n\n 0 \r\n GROUPS\n\n Departmental\nResearch Groups\n\n 0 \r\n COLLABORATIONS\n\n International Collaborations\n in 60 Countries for Research\n\n Core Research Domains\n\n Artificial Intelligence\n\n Research in AI concentrates on building systems that can perceive their environment, interpret data and make autonomous decisions. Efforts include work on cognitive models, deep learning frameworks and intelligent agents designed to elevate efficiency, shape the future of automated solutions and more.\n\n Machine Learning\n\n Machine learning research explores models that recognize patterns, learn from data and continually refine their performance. The domain focuses on predictive analytics, adaptive algorithms, learning techniques that empower technology to solve data intensive challenges with precision and more.\n\n Biotechnology\n\n Biotechnology research examines the mechanisms of living systems to develop applications that advance healthcare and sustainable development. Work spans genetic tools, cellular engineering, molecular innovation, and more aimed at improving human wellbeing and strengthening biological industries.\n\n Material Science\n\n Research in material science investigates how matter behaves and how new materials can be engineered for superior performance. The focus ranges from structural materials to smart composites with properties that drive progress in energy, electronics and next generation manufacturing.\n\n Robotics\n\n The robotics domain advances systems capable of intelligent movement, perception and autonomous action. Research covers robotic design, control systems and interactions that enable machines to function reliably in dynamic environments and assist in real world operations.\n\n Quantum Computing\n\n Quantum computing research explores computational principles based on quantum states to achieve capabilities beyond classical limits. Work involves quantum algorithms, error management, secure quantum communication and more.\n\n Bioinformatics\n\n Bioinformatics integrates biological data with computational power to decode complex biological processes. Research focuses on genome interpretation, molecular simulations and analytical pipelines that accelerate scientific understanding and support personalized healthcare.\n\n Microelectronics\n\n Microelectronics research develops compact, high efficiency electronic components that form the backbone of modern technology. Areas of focus include semiconductor development, circuit innovation and system miniaturization that enhance device performance across industries.\n\n Forensics\n\n Forensic research applies scientific techniques to uncover evidence and deliver accurate interpretations in investigative contexts. Work spans digital analysis, biological examination and trace detection methods that contribute to reliable justice and informed decision making.\n\n Nanotechnology\n\n Nanotechnology research examines materials and phenomena at the atomic scale to create highly specialized solutions. Work includes nanoscale fabrication, targeted delivery systems and engineered nanomaterials that revolutionize healthcare, energy and advanced device development.\n\n Programs Offered\n\n Applications are invited for admission to Full Time and Part Time Ph.D.\n (January 2026 Intake) Programmes under various disciplines\n\n Level of Study:\n\n Doctorate Programs \r\n\n List of Ph.D Programs\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Pharmaceutical Sciences) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-bio-pharma.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Computer Applications) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-computer-applications.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Electrical Engineering) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-electrical-engineering.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Mechanical Engineering) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-mechanical-engineering.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Physics) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-physics.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Computer Science Engineering) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-computer-science.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Mass-Communication) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-mass-communication.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Tourism and Hospitality Management) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-tourism-and-hospitality-management.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (English) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-english.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Zoology) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-zoology.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Botany) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-botany.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Nutrition & Dietetics) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-nutrition-dietetics.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Commerce) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-commerce.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Education) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-education.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Design) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-design.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Economics) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-economics.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Physical Education) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-physical-education.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Biotech) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-biotech.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Chemistry) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-chemistry.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Business Management) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-business-management.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Mathematics) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-mathematics.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Civil Engineering) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-civil-engineering.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Electronics & Communication Engineering) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-electronics-and-communication.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Law) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-law.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Architecture) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-architecture.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Physiotherapy) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-physiotherapy.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Medical Lab Technology) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-medical-lab-technology.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Microbiology) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-microbiology.php)\n\n Doctorate of Philosophy (Emerging Technologies & Intelligent Systems) (https://www.cuchd.in/doctorate-programs/phd-emerging-tech-and-intelligent-systems.php)\n\n Proud Hub of Researchers\n Ranked Among The World’s Top 2% Scientists (Stanford Global List 2024) \n\n Dr. Jashanpreet Singh\n\n Assistant Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 90+ Research Publications\n\n Key contributions in thermal spray coatings, and tribology\n\n Dr. Meet Kumari\n\n Assistant Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 120+ Research Articles\n\n Key contributions in Photonics, Optical Communication Networks\n\n Dr. Mohammad Ashfaq\n\n Assistant Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 91+ Research Articles\n\n Key contributions in Nanotechnology & Biomedical Applications\n\n Dr. Mehtab Singh\n\n Assistant Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 150+ Research Papers\n\n Key contributions in optical communication systems & photonic radars\n\n Dr. Deepak Kukkar\n\n Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 75 Research Articles\n\n Key contributions in Biosensing of CKD Biomarkers & Environmental Pollutants\n\n Dr. Kaushik\n\n Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 240+ Research Articles\n\n Key contributions in Nanofabrication, Bio-inspired Materials, Green Nanotechnology\n\n Dr. Atul Kabra\n\n Associate Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 90+ Research Publications\n\n Key contributions on pharmacology, focusing on neurodegenerative diseases & herbal drug development\n\n Dr. Hitesh K. Dewangan\n\n Associate Professor\nChandigarh University \r\n\n 75+ Research Publications\n\n Key contributions in pharmaceutics focusing Nanovaccine & Formulation development\n\n Seasoned professionals provide \n real-world knowledge and applied learning \n\n Step Into the Future with Guidance from Proven Practitioners!\n\n Professors of Practice (https://www.cuchd.in/professors-of-practice/)\r\n\n Nobel Laureates Driving Thought-Provoking \n Dialogues on Scientific Disruption\n\n I am quite impressed as educational institutions like Chandigarh University have filed so many patents in different domains. A researcher is essentially a learner who continues his learning process forever. AI is a very powerful tool but it’s not magic and it will change many more things, one must be optimistic about it.\n\n Prof. (Dr.) Jean-Marie Lehn\n\n Nobel Laureate in Chemistry & Professor of Chemistry, University of Strasbourg Institute for Advanced Study (USIAS) \r\n\n Chandigarh University’s vision and history are really impressive. Language is a tool that is used to communicate thoughts and ideas from one society to another, and when it is communicated, then there might be a change in the essence of what you really want to communicate. With times and changing technology, language also tends to evolve by adding new vocabulary or words but the purity of language needs to be maintained.\n\n Prof. (Dr.) Wole Soyinka\n\n Nobel Laureate in Literature \r\n\n Being a young university, huge admiration for Chandigarh University for the level of achievement made so far. The interest for pure sciences must be nurtured, as a new invention or discovery can be made only after studying physics, biology or chemistry. As a student you should never give-up the unique learning tool of being inquisitive or being curious.\n\n Prof. (Dr.) Michel Mayor\n\n Nobel Laureate in Physics & Swiss Astrophysicist \r\n\n The situation of crisis throws open new challenges and opportunities. The researchers are working on the problem to help the countries combating the climate change situation which is affecting humans, animals and plants all over the world. It is very important that you find something that you are really passionate about.\n\n Prof. (Dr.) Richard J. Roberts\n\n Nobel Laureate in Physiology or Medicine \r\n\n Government and \n Industry-Funded Projects\n\n 01 \r\n\n Identification of novel diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers\n\n Identification of novel diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers\n\n Metagenomic and bioinformatic analysis of gut microbiota from Diabetic Nephropathy patients to identify novel diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers.\n\n 02 \r\n\n Exploring the Determinants of CBDC Adoption\n\n Exploring the Determinants of Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) Adoption\n\n Exploring the Determinants of CBDC Adoption: The Moderating Role of the Unified Payments Interface (UPI) Experience in India.\n\n 03 \r\n\n Empowering Women in the Unorganized Sector\n\n Empowering Women in the Unorganized Sector\n\n A Study on the Impact of MUDRA Loans under the Pradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana in India\n\n 04 \r\n\n Detection of urinary neutrophil gelatinase-associated lipocalin\n\n Detection of urinary neutrophil gelatinase-associated lipocalin\n\n Development of fluorescent carbon dots-based point-of-care biosensor for the detection of urinary neutrophil gelatinase-associated lipocalin.\n\n 05 \r\n\n Elucidating the role of DNA methylation under elevated CO₂\n\n Elucidating the role of DNA methylation under elevated CO₂\n\n Elucidating the role of DNA methylation under elevated CO₂ and temperature during grain filling in Wheat (Triticum aestivum L.).\n\n Government Collaborators\n\n Esteemed\n Industry Partners \n\n World-Class \nResearch Infrastructure\n\n Apple Vision Pro Lab\n\n Know More (https://www.cuchd.in/phd-me-admissions/ApplicationRegistration.aspx?Subject=fJAt3RX8ggEX//eDGysKyA==) \r\n\n Experience Lounge Powered by Adobe\n\n Know More (https://www.cuchd.in/phd-me-admissions/ApplicationRegistration.aspx?Subject=fJAt3RX8ggEX//eDGysKyA==) \r\n\n LinkedIn Experience Zone\n\n Know More (https://www.cuchd.in/phd-me-admissions/ApplicationRegistration.aspx?Subject=fJAt3RX8ggEX//eDGysKyA==) \r\n\n CoE in Advanced Computing Technologies – Paloalto\n\n Know More (https://www.cuchd.in/phd-me-admissions/Applicatio