n Get to know MDN better\n\n About MDN\n \n Advertise with us\n\n Community\n \n MDN on GitHub\n\n Blog\n\n Toggle sidebar \n\n Web\n\n Web APIs\n\n ServiceWorkerRegistration\n\n installing\n\n Theme \n\n OS default \n\n Light \n\n Dark \n\n English (US) \n\n Remember language (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML)\n Learn more \n\n Deutsch \n\n English (US) \n\n 日本語 \n\n 한국어 \n\n ServiceWorkerRegistration: installing property\n\n Baseline\n \n Widely available\n\n This feature is well established and works across many devices and browser versions. It’s been available across browsers since April 2018.\n\n See full compatibility (https://developer.mozilla.org/de/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerRegistration/installing)\n\n Learn more (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Baseline/Compatibility)\n\n Secure context: This feature is available only in secure contexts (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Defenses/Secure_Contexts) (HTTPS), in some or all supporting browsers .\n\n Note: This feature is available in Web Workers (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Workers_API).\n\n The installing read-only property of the\nServiceWorkerRegistration (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerRegistration) interface returns a service worker whose\nServiceWorker.state (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorker/state) is installing . This property is\ninitially set to null .\n\n In this article\n\n Value \n\n Specifications \n\n Browser compatibility \n\n See also \n\n Value \n\n A ServiceWorker (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorker) object, if it is currently in an installing \nstate.\n\n Specifications \n\n Specification\n\n Service Workers Nightly \n# navigator-service-worker-installing \n\n Browser compatibility \n\n See also \n\n Using Service Workers (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API/Using_Service_Workers)\n\n Service w