s/)\n\n News (https://www.w3.org/news/)\n\n Blog (https://www.w3.org/blog/)\n\n Press releases (https://www.w3.org/press-releases/)\n\n Press & media (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Events (https://www.w3.org/events/)\n\n Annual W3C Conference (TPAC) (https://www.w3.org/news-events/tpac/)\n\n Code of conduct (https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Support us\n\n Make a huge difference to our operations as a public-interest non-profit, and help us to achieve our vision.\n\n Ways you can support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n About (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n About\n\n Understand our values and principles, learn our history, look into our policies, meet our people.\n\n Find out more about us (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n Our mission (https://www.w3.org/mission/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Leadership (https://www.w3.org/about/leadership/)\n\n Staff (https://www.w3.org/staff/)\n\n Careers (https://www.w3.org/careers/)\n\n Media kit (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Diversity (https://www.w3.org/about/diversity/)\n\n Corporation (https://www.w3.org/about/corporation/)\n\n Policies & legal information (https://www.w3.org/policies/)\n\n Contact us (https://www.w3.org/contact/)\n\n Help (https://www.w3.org/help/)\n\n Search (https://www.w3.org/help/search/)\n\n My account (https://www.w3.org/users/myprofile/)\n\n Home (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Get involved (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/)\n\n Promote web standards (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/promote/)\n\n Promote web standards\n\n Read this page in: \n\n 中文（简体） (https://www.w3.org/zh-hans/get-involved/promote/)\n\n 日本語 (https://www.w3.org/ja/get-involved/promote/)\n\n Page contents\n\n Translations \n\n Using standards \n\n Logos and icons \n\n Education and outreach \n\n In addition to attending W3C events (https://www.w3.org/events/) such as Workshops (https://www.w3.org/events/workshops/) and Talks (https://www.w3.org/events/talks/), supporters of open, royalty-free standards can help promote web technologies through the activities listed below.\n\n Translations\n\n The W3C community provides a great service through volunteer translations (https://www.w3.org/Translations/) of technical reports and other documentation. You can search the translations database (https://www.w3.org/2005/11/Translations/TranslationSearch.html) and volunteer (https://www.w3.org/Translations/) your own translation (or collaborate with someone else wishing to translate the same document).\n\n Using standards\n\n W3C makes a number of tools (https://www.w3.org/QA/Tools) available to help people build sites that work with standards. The most popular is the W3C validator service (https://validator.w3.org/) but we encourage you to check the other checkers as well.\n\n Logos and icons\n\n We invite you to show your support for standards by displaying the W3C icon or any of the many other logos made available by W3C; please see the W3C logo usage policy (https://www.w3.org/policies/logos/).\n\n Education and outreach\n\n W3C has chartered groups to conduct education and outreach in these areas:\n\n Accessibility (https://www.w3.org/WAI/EO/)\n\n Internationalization \n\n In this section\n\n Promote web standards (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/promote/)\n\n TPAC inclusion fund (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/tpac-inclusion-fund/)\n\n Home (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Contact (https://www.w3.org/contact/)\n\n Help (https://www.w3.org/help/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Legal & Policies (https://www.w3.org/policies/)\n\n Corporation (https://www.w3.org/about/corporation/)\n\n System Status (https://status.w3.org/)\n\n W3C on Mastodon (https://w3c.social/@w3c)\n\n W3C on GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/)\n\n Copyright &copy; 2026 World Wide Web Consortium (https://www.w3.org/).\n W3C &reg; liability , trademark and permissive license (https://www.w3.org/copyright/document-license/) rules apply.','c35a21629bebf93e991d6d0e14dc381d458b150455b568beac9f09db9b1b43a5',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-05 07:46:09','INDEXED','2026-10-05 07:41:28','2026-10-05 07:46:09'),(869,7,36,'218bd0da026f0167501452cf7294ad24958b9c5a103b47f9bd3d53e753ffae6e','https://www.w3.org/liaisons/','Liaisons | W3C','Liaisons | W3C \n\n Skip to content \n\n 日本語ホームページJapanese website (https://www.w3.org/ja/)\n\n 简体中文首页Chinese website (https://www.w3.org/zh-hans/)\n\n Visit the W3C homepage (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Standards & groups (https://www.w3.org/standards/)\n\n Standards & groups\n\n Understand the various specifications, their maturity levels on the web standards track, their adoption, and the groups that develop them.\n\n Explore web standards (https://www.w3.org/standards/)\n\n About W3C web standards (https://www.w3.org/standards/about/)\n\n W3C standards & drafts (https://www.w3.org/TR/)\n\n Types of documents W3C publishes (https://www.w3.org/standards/types/)\n\n W3C groups (https://www.w3.org/groups/)\n\n Translations of W3C standards & drafts (https://www.w3.org/translations/)\n\n Reviews & public feedback (https://www.w3.org/standards/review/)\n\n Promote web standards (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/promote/)\n\n Liaisons (https://www.w3.org/liaisons/)\n\n Technical Architecture Group (TAG) (https://www.w3.org/groups/other/tag/)\n\n Get involved (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/)\n\n Get involved\n\n W3C works at the nexus of core technology, industry needs, and societal needs.\n\n Find ways to get involved (https://www.w3.org/get-involved/)\n\n Browse our work by industry (https://www.w3.org/ecosystems/)\n\n Become a Member (https://www.w3.org/membership/)\n\n Member home (restricted) (https://www.w3.org/Member/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Mailing lists (https://www.w3.org/email/)\n\n Participant guidebook (https://www.w3.org/guide/)\n\n Positive work environment (https://www.w3.org/about/positive-work-environment/)\n\n Invited Experts (https://www.w3.org/invited-experts/)\n\n Resources (https://www.w3.org/resources/)\n\n Resources\n\n Master web fundamentals, use our developer tools, or contribute code.\n\n Learn from W3C resources (https://www.w3.org/resources/)\n\n Developers (https://www.w3.org/developers/)\n\n Validators & tools (https://www.w3.org/developers/tools/)\n\n Accessibility fundamentals (https://www.w3.org/WAI/fundamentals/)\n\n Internationalization (i18n) (https://www.w3.org/International/i18n-drafts/nav/about)\n\n Translations of W3C standards & drafts (https://www.w3.org/translations/)\n\n Code of conduct (https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/)\n\n Reports (https://www.w3.org/reports/)\n\n News & events (https://www.w3.org/news-events/)\n\n News & events\n\n Recent content across news, blogs, press releases, media; upcoming events.\n\n Explore news & events (https://www.w3.org/news-events/)\n\n News (https://www.w3.org/news/)\n\n Blog (https://www.w3.org/blog/)\n\n Press releases (https://www.w3.org/press-releases/)\n\n Press & media (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Events (https://www.w3.org/events/)\n\n Annual W3C Conference (TPAC) (https://www.w3.org/news-events/tpac/)\n\n Code of conduct (https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Support us\n\n Make a huge difference to our operations as a public-interest non-profit, and help us to achieve our vision.\n\n Ways you can support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n About (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n About\n\n Understand our values and principles, learn our history, look into our policies, meet our people.\n\n Find out more about us (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n Our mission (https://www.w3.org/mission/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Leadership (https://www.w3.org/about/leadership/)\n\n Staff (https://www.w3.org/staff/)\n\n Careers (https://www.w3.org/careers/)\n\n Media kit (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Diversity (https://www.w3.org/about/diversity/)\n\n Corporation (https://www.w3.org/about/corporation/)\n\n Policies & legal information (https://www.w3.org/policies/)\n\n Contact us (https://www.w3.org/contact/)\n\n Help (https://www.w3.org/help/)\n\n Search (https://www.w3.org/help/search/)\n\n My account (https://www.w3.org/users/myprofile/)\n\n Home (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Liaisons (https://www.w3.org/liaisons/)\n\n Liaisons\n\n Read this page in: \n\n 中文（简体） (https://www.w3.org/zh-hans/liaisons/)\n\n 日本語 (https://www.w3.org/ja/liaisons/)\n\n Page contents\n\n Liaisons \n\n Mission of W3C international liaisons \n\n Contacting W3C to establish a liaison \n\n About the liaison table \n\n Considerations when establishing a liaison \n\n W3C and De Jure standards \n\n Many organizations in addition to W3C develop standards for the Internet or the Web. In order to coordinate the development of the Web, W3C engages in liaisons with numerous organizations after careful consideration of the costs and benefits .\n\n As defined in the W3C Process Document , the term \"liaison\" is used to refer to coordination of activities with a variety of organizations, through a number of mechanisms ranging from very informal to mutual membership, or even more formal agreements. Liaisons are not meant to substitute for W3C membership.\n\n W3C is a broad community which covers standardization work in W3C Working Groups and incubation work in W3C Community Groups (CGs). Listing a formal liaison with W3C on behalf of a CG on this page is generally discouraged because CG output does not represent the consensus of the W3C Community (of course informal liaison is always encouraged). If an external group outside of W3C would like a Liaison with a CG, they must write up their rationale and be explicit that they understand that the CG work is not normative. If there is such a request, it should be sent to team-liaisons@w3.org for approval.\n\n While this page is public, some links may be W3C member-only.\n\n Contact W3C about a new or existing liaison. \n\n Liaisons\n\n Liaison index: \n\n 3 • A • B • C • D • E • F • G • H • I • J • K • L • M • N • O • P • S • T • U • V • W \n\n Column one lists organizations, and then whether it has a MOU with W3C, activities in scope, the W3C contact and the liaison contact Organization MOU W3C activities affected W3C contact Liaison contact \n\n 3GPP 3rd Generation Partnership Project Media and Entertainment (https://www.w3.org/ecosystems/media/), SVG (https://www.w3.org/Graphics/SVG/), Timed Text (https://www.w3.org/AudioVideo/TT/) TBD (was Kazuyuki Ashimura), Chris Lilley , François Daoust , Philippe Le Hégaret 3GPP Liaison alias,\n\nAndrijana Brekalo (MCC, ETSI),\n\nSVG: Tolga Capin \n\n Accord Project (https://www.accordproject.org/) Verifiable claims, Blockchain TBD Peter Hunn \n\n ACM The Web Conference (https://sigweb.org/conferences/acm-sigweb-conferences/the-web-conference) Steering Committee Communications (https://www.w3.org/) Pierre-Antoine Champin Dick Bulterman \n\n Annotating All Knowledge Coalition (https://hypothes.is/annotating-all-knowledge/) (Steering Committee) Digital Publishing Ivan Herman Maryann Martone, Dan Whaley \n\n Access Board (US) WAI (https://www.w3.org/WAI/) Shawn Lawton Henry Sachin Pavithran, Ph.D. \n\n Assistive Technology Industry Association (ATIA) (https://www.atia.org/) WAI (https://www.w3.org/WAI/) Shawn Lawton Henry David Dikter \n\n Alliance for Internet of Things Innovation (AIOTI) (https://www.aioti.eu/) Web of Things (https://www.w3.org/ecosystems/web-of-things/) Dave Raggett Patrick Guillemin \n\n Apache (https://www.apache.org/) The Apache Software Foundation Open Source (https://www.w3.org/Status) TBD Apache board \n\n Association of Radio Industries and Businesses (ARIB) (https://www.arib.or.jp/) Media and Entertainment (https://www.w3.org/ecosystems/media/), Timed Text (https://www.w3.org/AudioVideo/TT/) Philippe Le Hégaret \n\nTBD (was Kazuyuki Ashimura) Hisayuki Oomata