.w3.org/WAI/fundamentals/)\n\n Internationalization (i18n) (https://www.w3.org/International/i18n-drafts/nav/about)\n\n Translations of W3C standards & drafts (https://www.w3.org/translations/)\n\n Code of conduct (https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/)\n\n Reports (https://www.w3.org/reports/)\n\n News & events (https://www.w3.org/news-events/)\n\n News & events\n\n Recent content across news, blogs, press releases, media; upcoming events.\n\n Explore news & events (https://www.w3.org/news-events/)\n\n News (https://www.w3.org/news/)\n\n Blog (https://www.w3.org/blog/)\n\n Press releases (https://www.w3.org/press-releases/)\n\n Press & media (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Events (https://www.w3.org/events/)\n\n Annual W3C Conference (TPAC) (https://www.w3.org/news-events/tpac/)\n\n Code of conduct (https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Support us\n\n Make a huge difference to our operations as a public-interest non-profit, and help us to achieve our vision.\n\n Ways you can support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n About (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n About\n\n Understand our values and principles, learn our history, look into our policies, meet our people.\n\n Find out more about us (https://www.w3.org/about/)\n\n Our mission (https://www.w3.org/mission/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Leadership (https://www.w3.org/about/leadership/)\n\n Staff (https://www.w3.org/staff/)\n\n Careers (https://www.w3.org/careers/)\n\n Media kit (https://www.w3.org/about/press-media/)\n\n Diversity (https://www.w3.org/about/diversity/)\n\n Corporation (https://www.w3.org/about/corporation/)\n\n Policies & legal information (https://www.w3.org/policies/)\n\n Contact us (https://www.w3.org/contact/)\n\n Help (https://www.w3.org/help/)\n\n Search (https://www.w3.org/help/search/)\n\n My account (https://www.w3.org/users/myprofile/)\n\n Home (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Developers (https://www.w3.org/developers/)\n\n Validators and tools (https://www.w3.org/developers/tools/)\n\n Validators and tools\n\n Read this page in: \n\n 中文（简体） (https://www.w3.org/zh-hans/developers/tools/)\n\n 日本語 (https://www.w3.org/ja/developers/tools/)\n\n Make your code work — for everyone, with great and open source tools.\n\n  Nu HTML Checker\n\n Checks HTML documents.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/validator/validator) | Issues (https://github.com/validator/validator/issues)\n\n Nu HTML Checker (https://validator.w3.org/nu/)\n\n  Link Checker\n\n Checks your web pages for broken links.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/link-checker) | Issues (https://github.com/w3c/link-checker/issues)\n\n Link Checker (https://validator.w3.org/checklink)\n\n  Internationalization Checker\n\n Checks level of internationalization - friendliness.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/i18n-checker) | Issues (https://github.com/w3c/i18n-checker/issues)\n\n Internationalization Checker (https://validator.w3.org/i18n-checker/)\n\n EPUBCheck\n\n The conformance checker for EPUB publications.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/epubcheck) | Issues (https://github.com/w3c/epubcheck/issues)\n\n EPUBCheck (https://www.w3.org/publishing/epubcheck/)\n\n CSS Validator\n\n Checks your Cascading Style Sheets (CSS).\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/css-validator) | Issues (https://github.com/w3c/css-validator/issues)\n\n CSS Validator (https://jigsaw.w3.org/css-validator/)\n\n RDF Validator\n\n Checks and visualizes RDF documents.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/rdfvalidator-ng) | Issues (https://github.com/w3c/rdfvalidator-ng/issues)\n\n RDF Validator (https://www.w3.org/RDF/Validator/)\n\n RSS Feed Validator\n\n Validator for syndicated feeds (RSS and Atom feeds).\n\n RSS Feed Validator (https://validator.w3.org/feed/)\n\n Web Platform Tests\n\n Test and help the interoperability of the Web.\n\n GitHub (https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) | Issues (https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues)\n\n Web Platform Tests (https://web-platform-tests.org/)\n\n W3C API\n\n We are now making available public data on Specifications, Groups, Organizations and Users. We are providing a JSON format initially with alternate formats in the works and we will be expanding what information we expose over time.\n\n More information on Github (https://github.com/w3c/w3c-api/)\n\n  Get help\n\n Stack Overflow (https://stackoverflow.com/) has a great and active community focused around W3C Standards and W3C developer tools.\nTo ask a question to the W3C Community, we invite you to use the w3c tag.\n\n Ask a question (https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/w3c)\n\n Contribute\n\n Developers are welcome to get involved by contributing code, either to existing tools or proposed future projects.\n\n Testing, bug reports, suggestions, or help in creating good documentation are also important!\n\n You will find more information to get started in each project on their own web page.\n\n Find projects on Github (https://github.com/w3c/)\n\n Donate\n\n Good tools cost a lot to develop, support, host and maintain.\n\n With your help, we can make the tools and validators better, faster, friendlier, and maintain a great, free service for all of the Web.\n\n Donate now (https://www.w3.org/donate/)\n\n Home (https://www.w3.org/)\n\n Contact (https://www.w3.org/contact/)\n\n Help (https://www.w3.org/help/)\n\n Support us (https://www.w3.org/support-us/)\n\n Legal & Policies (https://www.w3.org/policies/)\n\n Corporation (https://www.w3.org/about/corporation/)\n\n System Status (https://status.w3.org/)\n\n W3C on Mastodon (https://w3c.social/@w3c)\n\n W3C on GitHub (https://github.com/w3c/)\n\n Copyright &copy; 2026 World Wide Web Consortium (https://www.w3.org/).\n W3C &reg; liability , trademark and permissive license (https://www.w3.org/copyright/document-license/) rules apply.','fc9447042cea995f904000d55d04706f61adc8c8f5bcb1fce31ddb855c5424a8',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-05 07:46:09','INDEXED','2026-10-05 07:41:28','2026-10-05 07:46:09');
