es (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_exercises.php)\nC Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_quiz.php)\nC Code Challenges (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_challenges.php)\nC Practice Problems (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_practice.php)\nC Compiler (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_compiler.php)\nC Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_syllabus.php)\nC Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_study_plan.php)\nC Interview Q&A (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_interview_questions.php)\n\n C Tutorial \n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_intro.php)\n\n Learn C\n\n C is a general-purpose programming language that has been widely used for over 50 years.\n\n C is very powerful; it has been used to develop operating systems, databases, applications, etc.\n\n Learn C now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_intro.php)\n\n Become C Certified\n\n Get certified with our C exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-c)\n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Examples in Each Chapter\n\n Our \"Try it Yourself\" editor makes it easy to learn C. You can edit code and view \nthe result in your browser:\n\n Example\n\n #include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n printf(\"Hello World!\");\n \n return 0;\n}\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/c/tryc.php?filename=demo_helloworld)\n\n C Exercises\n\n Many chapters in this tutorial end with an exercise where you can check your level of knowledge.\n\n See all C Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_exercises.php)\n\n What You\'ll Learn\n\n This tutorial will guide you step by step, with examples and exercises along the way:\n\n How C programs are structured\n\n Variables, data types, and operators\n\n If statements, loops, and arrays\n\n Functions and how to reuse code\n\n Pointers and memory\n\n Structures to organize related data\n\n Reading from and writing to files\n\n Organizing programs and build real-life projects\n\n C Quiz\n\n Check your understanding with a short quiz and see how well you know the basics of C.\n\n Start C Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_quiz.php)\n\n Learn by Examples\n\n Learn by examples! This tutorial supplements all explanations with clarifying examples.\n\n See All C Examples (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_examples.php)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n C Reference\n\n You will also find complete keyword and function references:\n\n Reference Overview (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_reference.php)\n C Keywords (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_keywords.php)\n C stdio Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_stdio.php)\n C stdlib Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_stdlib.php)\n C string Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_string.php)\n C math Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_math.php)\n C ctype Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_ctype.php)\n C time Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/c/c_ref_time.php)\n\n Course Certification\n\n Get Certified in coding \n\n Complete the W3Schools coding course, strengthen your knowledge, and earn a certificate you can add to your CV, portfolio, and LinkedIn profile.\n\n Get Certified Today (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog)\n\n W3Schools Certificate\n Coding\n \n Learn it. Practice it. Prove it. (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog)\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ 