mpiler.asp)\nReact Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_quiz.asp)\nReact Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_exercises.asp)\nReact Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_syllabus.asp)\nReact Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_study_plan.asp)\nReact Server (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_server.asp)\nReact Interview Prep (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_interview_prep.asp)\n\n React Tutorial\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_intro.asp)\n\n Learn React\n\n React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces.\n\n React is used to build single-page applications.\n\n React allows us to create reusable UI components.\n\n Learn React now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_intro.asp)\n\n Become React Certified\n\n Get certified with our React exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/react-js-course)\n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Learning by Examples\n\n Our \"Show React\" tool makes it easy to demonstrate React. It shows both the code and the result.\n\n Example:\n\n import { createRoot } from \'react-dom/client\';\n\nfunction Hello() {\n return (\n <h1>Hello World!</h1>\n );\n}\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')).render(\n <Hello />\n);\n\nRun \nExample &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/react/showreact.asp?filename=demo_default)\n\n Learning by Exercises\n\n Many chapters in this tutorial end with an exercise where you can check you level of knowledge.\n\n See all React Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_exercises.asp)\n\n React Quiz\n\n Test your React skills with a quiz.\n\n React Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/react/react_quiz.asp)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, 