/www.w3schools.com/django/django_ref_filter.php)\nField lookups Reference (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_ref_field_lookups.php)\n\n Django Exercises\n\nDjango Compiler (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_compiler.php)\nDjango Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_exercises.php)\nDjango Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_quiz.php)\nDjango Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_syllabus.php)\nDjango Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_study_plan.php)\nDjango Server (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_server.php)\n\n Django Tutorial\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_intro.php)\n\n Learn Django\n\n Django is a back-end server side web framework.\n\n Django is free, open source and written in Python.\n\n Django makes it easier to build web pages using Python.\n\n Learn Django now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_intro.php)\n\n Become Django Certified\n\n Get certified with our Django exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-django)\n\n Certified Django Developer \n The candidate has passed the exam at the Professional level. \n Verify at \n verify.w3schools.com \n Stale Refsnes \n for w3schools.com \n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Learning by Doing\n\nIn this tutorial you get a step by step guide on how to install and create a Django project.\nYou will learn how to create a project where you can add, read, update or delete data.\n\nYou will learn how to make HTML Templates and use Django Template Tags to insert data within a HTML document.\n\nYou will learn how to work with QuerySets to extract, filter, and sort data from the database.\n\nYou will also learn how to set up a PostgreSQL database and how to deploy your \nDjango project to the world.\n\n Django\n\nIntroduction (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_intro.php)\n\nGetting Started (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_getstarted.php)\n\nVirtual Environment (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_create_virtual_environment.php)\n\nInstall Django (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_install_django.php)\n\nCreate Project (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_create_project.php)\n\nCreate App (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_create_app.php)\n\nViews (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_views.php)\n\nUrls (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_urls.php)\n\nTemplates (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_templates.php)\n\nModels (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_models.php)\n\nInsert Data (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_insert_data.php)\n\nUpdate Data (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_update_data.php)\n\nDelete Data (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_delete_data.php)\n\nUpdate Model (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_update_model.php)\n\n Display\n\nPrepare (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_prepare_template.php)\n\nAdd Details (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_add_link_details.php)\n\nAdd Master (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_master_template.php)\n\nAdd Main (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_add_main.php)\n\nAdd 404 (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_404.php)\n\nAdd Test (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_test_view.php)\n\n Admin\n\nAdmin (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin.php)\n\nCreate User (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_create_user.php)\n\nModels (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_include_members.php)\n\nList Display (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_set_list_display.php)\n\nUpdate (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_update_members.php)\n\nAdd (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_add_members.php)\n\nDelete (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_admin_delete_members.php)\n\n Syntax\n\nVariables (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_template_variables.php)\n\nTags (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_template_tags.php)\n\nIf...Else (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_tags_if.php)\n\nFor Loop (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_tags_for.php)\n\nComment (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_tags_comment.php)\n\nInclude (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_tags_include.php)\n\n QuerySets\n\nQuerySet (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_queryset.php)\n\nGet Data (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_queryset_get.php)\n\nFilter (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_queryset_filter.php)\n\nOrder By (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_queryset_orderby.php)\n\n Static Files\n\nAdd Static (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_add_static_files.php)\n\nWhiteNoise (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_static_whitenoise.php)\n\nCollect (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_collect_static_files.php)\n\nGlobal Static (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_add_global_static_files.php)\n\nAdd to Poject (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_add_css_file_project.php)\n\n PostgreSQL\n\nIntro (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_db_postgresql_intro.php)\n\nAWS Account (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_db_create_aws_account.php)\n\nRDS (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_db_create_rds.php)\n\nConnect (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_db_connect.php)\n\nAdd Members (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_db_add_members.php)\n\n Deploy\n\nElastic Beanstalk (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_provider.php)\n\nRequirements (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_requirements.php)\n\ndjango.config (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_config.php)\n\nCreate .zip (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_zip.php)\n\nDeploy (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_eb.php)\n\nUpdate (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_deploy_update.php)\n\n Learning by Examples\n\n In the tutorial we will use examples to better explain the various concepts.\n\n Example\n\n <ul>\n {% for x in mymembers %}\n <li>{{ x.firstname }}</li>\n {% endfor %}\n</ul> \nRun Example &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/django/showdjango.php?filename=demo_django_index)\n\n Learning by Exercises\n\n Many chapters in this tutorial end with an exercise where you can check your level of knowledge.\n\n See all Django Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_exercises.php)\n\n Django Quiz\n\n Learn by taking a quiz! The quiz will give you a signal of how much you know about Django.\n\n Start Django Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_quiz.php)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n Learning by References\n\n You will also find references over the most common Django features:\n\n Template Tags (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_ref_template_tags.php)\n QuerySet Filters (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_ref_filter.php)\n Field Lookups (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_ref_field_lookups.php)\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/django/django_intro.php)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n Learn more about Adventure Mode&rsaquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/adventure/)\n\n Free account\n\n Track you