r Forms (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_forms.asp)\nAngular Router (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_router.asp)\nAngular Services & DI (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_services.asp)\nAngular HTTP Client (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_http.asp)\nAngular Pipes (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_pipes.asp)\nAngular Lifecycle Hooks (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_lifecycle.asp)\nAngular Styling (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_css_styling.asp)\n\n Advanced Angular\n\nAngular App Bootstrap (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_app_bootstrap.asp)\nAngular Control Flow (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_control_flow.asp)\nAngular Signals (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_signals.asp)\nAngular Change Detection (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_change_detection.asp)\nAngular Dynamic Comp (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_dynamic_components.asp)\nAngular Advanced DI (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_di_advanced.asp)\nAngular Router Advanced (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_router_advanced.asp)\nAngular HTTP Interceptors (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_http_interceptors.asp)\nAngular Forms Advanced (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_forms_reactive_advanced.asp)\nAngular State Management (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_state_management.asp)\nAngular Animations (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_animations.asp)\nAngular Testing (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_testing.asp)\nAngular Security (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_security.asp)\nAngular SSR & Hydration (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_ssr_hydration.asp)\n\n Angular Exercises\n\nAngular Compiler (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_compiler.asp)\nAngular Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_exercises.asp)\nAngular Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_quiz.asp)\nAngular Server (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_server.asp)\n\n Angular Tutorial\n\n ❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\n Next ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_intro.asp)\n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Learn Angular\n\n Angular is a framework for building client applications in HTML and TypeScript.\n\n Start learning Angular now &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_intro.asp)\n\n Overview & Prerequisites\n\n Learn Angular step-by-step with easy-to-follow pages and runnable JS-only examples.\n\n We use standalone components, modern control flow, and the built-in Router and HttpClient in examples.\n\n Prerequisites: \n\n Basic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n\n Some TypeScript helps but is not required.\n\n Learning by Examples\n\n Our \"Show Angular\" tool makes it easy to demonstrate Angular.\n\n It shows both the code and the result.\n\n Example:\n\n import { bootstrapApplication } from \'@angular/platform-browser\';\nimport { Component } from \'@angular/core\';\n\n@Component({\n selector: \'app-root\',\n standalone: true,\n template: `<h1>Hello Angular!</h1>`\n})\nexport class App {}\n\nbootstrapApplication(App); \n <!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n <title>Angular App</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n <app-root></app-root>\n</body>\n</html> \n \n Run \n Example &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/showangular.asp?filename=demo_default)\n\n Learning by Exercises\n\n Many chapters in this tutorial end with an exercise where you can check you level of knowledge.\n\n See all Angular Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_exercises.asp)\n\n Angular Quiz\n\n Test your Angular skills with a quiz.\n\n Angular Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/angular_quiz.asp)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\