it_lfs.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Signing Commits/Tags (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_signing.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Cherrypick & Patch (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_cherrypick_patch.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Merge Conflicts (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_merge_conflicts.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit CI/CD (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_cicd.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Hooks (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_hooks.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Submodules (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_submodules.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Remote Advanced (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_remote_advanced.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n Git Cert\n\nGit Certificate (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_exam.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n Git Exercises\n\nGit Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_exercises.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_quiz.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_syllabus.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nGit Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_study_plan.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n Git Tutorial \n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_intro.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n Learn Git\n\n Git is a free, open source tool that helps you save and manage different versions of your files and code.\n\n With Git, you can work with others, keep track of changes, and undo mistakes.\n\n Learn Git now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_intro.asp)\n\n Become Git Certified\n\n Get certified with our Git exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-git)\n\n Certified Git Developer \n The candidate has passed the exam at the Professional level. \n Verify at \n verify.w3schools.com \n Stale Refsnes \n for w3schools.com \n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Where to use Git?\n\n Git works on your computer, but you also use it with online services like GitHub , GitLab , or Bitbucket to share your work with others. These are called remote repositories .\n\n In this tutorial, you\'ll learn how to use Git for your own projects and how to connect with remote repositories online.\n\n Learning by Examples\n\n In this tutorial, we will show you Git commands like this:\n\n Example\n\n git --version\ngit version 2.30.2.windows.1 \n\n For new users, using the terminal view can seem a bit complicated.\n\n Don\'t worry! We will keep it really simple, and learning this way gives you a good grasp of how Git works.\n\n In the code above, you can see commands (input) and output.\n\n Lines like this are commands we input:\n\n Example\n\n git --version \n\n Lines like this are the output/response to our commands:\n\n Example\n\n git version 2.30.2.windows.1 \n\n In general, lines with $ in front of it is input.\n\n These are the commands you can copy and run in your terminal.\n\n Tip for Beginners: Don\'t worry about making mistakes!\n\n When you use Git on your own computer, you can\'t really break anything important.\n\n Experimenting is a great way to learn, and you can always undo or redo changes as you go.\n\n Change Platform:\n\nGitHub (https://www.w3schools.com/git/default.asp?remote=github)\nBitbucket (https://www.w3schools.com/git/default.asp?remote=bitbucket)\nGitLab (https://www.w3schools.com/git/default.asp?remote=gitlab)\n\n What Changes When You Switch Platform?\n\n The tutorial can show examples for GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket.\n\n The Git commands are mostly the same, but some steps (like connecting to a remote or pushing code) might look a little different depending on the platform you choose.\n\n Use the menu to see examples for each platform.\n\n Why Practice with Exercises?\n\n Practicing with exercises helps you remember the commands and understand how Git works.\n\n Try the exercises and quiz to test your knowledge!\n\n Git Quiz\n\n Test your Git skills with a quiz.\n\n Start Git Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_quiz.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/git/git_intro.asp?remote={{remoteName}})\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n Learn more about Adventure Mode&rsaquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/adventure/)\n\n Free account\n\n Track your progress\n\n XP earned 0 \n Day streak 0 \n Spaces 0 \n League &mdash; \n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n New\n\n Learn in Adventure Mode \n W3Schools Adventure App \n\n Coding fundamentals as bite-sized lessons and challenges.\n\n PLUS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n SPACES (https://www.w3schools.com/spaces/index.php)\n\n GET CERTIFIED (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/certifications)\n\n FOR TEACHERS (https://www.w3schools.com/academy/index.php)\n\n PRACTICE (https://www.w3schools.com/practice/index.php)\n\n CONTACT US\n\n &times; \n Contact Sales\n\n If you want to use W3Schools services as an educational institution, team or enterprise, send us an e-mail:\nsales@w3schools.com