://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-postgresql)\n\n Certified PostgreSQL Developer \n The candidate has passed the exam at the Professional level. \n Verify at \n verify.w3schools.com \n Stale Refsnes \n for w3schools.com \n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Learning by Doing\n\nIn this tutorial you get a step by step guide on how to install and create a PostgreSQL database.\nYou will learn how to create a project where you can create, read, update, and delete data.\n\nYou will learn how to query, filter, and sort data from the database.\n\n Examples in Each Chapter\n\n In the tutorial we will use examples to show what SQL statements returns from the database:\n\n Example\n\n Sort the table by year:\n\n SELECT * FROM cars\n\n ORDER BY year;\n\n Run Example &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/postgresql/trypostgresql.php?filename=demo_order_by) \n\n Learning by Exercises\n\n Many chapters in this tutorial end with an exercise where you can check your level of knowledge.\n\n See all PostgreSQL Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/postgresql/postgresql_exercises.php)\n\n PostgreSQL Quiz\n\n Learn by taking a quiz! The quiz will give you a signal of how much you know about PostgreSQL.\n\n Start PostgreSQL Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/postgresql/postgresql_quiz.php)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/postgresql/postgresql_intro.php)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url