n_ai/index.php)\n SCIPY (https://www.w3schools.com/python/scipy/index.php)\n CYBERSECURITY (https://www.w3schools.com/cybersecurity/index.php)\n DATA SCIENCE (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/default.asp)\n INTRO TO PROGRAMMING (https://www.w3schools.com/programming/index.php)\n HTML & CSS (https://www.w3schools.com/htmlcss/default.asp)\n BASH (https://www.w3schools.com/bash/index.php)\n RUST (https://www.w3schools.com/rust/index.php)\n TOOLS (https://www.w3schools.com/tools/index.php)\n\n MongoDB Tutorial\n\nMongoDB HOME (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/index.php)\nMongoDB Get Started (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_get_started.php)\nMongoDB Query API (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_query_api.php)\nMongoDB Create DB (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_create_database.php)\nMongoDB Collection (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_create_collection.php)\nMongoDB Insert (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_insert.php)\nMongoDB Find (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_find.php)\nMongoDB Update (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_update.php)\nMongoDB Delete (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_mongosh_delete.php)\nMongoDB Query Operators (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_query_operators.php)\nMongoDB Update Operators (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_update_operators.php)\nMongoDB Aggregations (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_intro.php)\n \n MongoDB Aggregations (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_intro.php)\n $group (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_group.php)\n $limit (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_limit.php)\n $project (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_project.php)\n $sort (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_sort.php)\n $match (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_match.php)\n $addFields (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_addFields.php)\n $count (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_count.php)\n $lookup (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_lookup.php)\n $out (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_aggregations_out.php)\n\nMongoDB Indexing/Search (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_indexing_search.php)\nMongoDB Validation (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_schema_validation.php)\nMongoDB Data API (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_data_api.php)\nMongoDB Drivers (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_drivers.php)\nMongoDB Node.js Driver (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_nodejs_connect_database.php)\nMongoDB Charts (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_charts.php)\n\n MongoDB Cert\n\nMongoDB Certificate (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_exam.php)\n\n MongoDB Exercises\n\nMongoDB Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_exercises.php)\nMongoDB Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_syllabus.php)\nMongoDB Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_study_plan.php)\n\n MongoDB Tutorial\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_get_started.php)\n\n Learn MongoDB\n\n MongoDB is a document database. It stores data in a type of JSON format called BSON.\n\n If you are unfamiliar with JSON, check out our JSON tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/js/js_json.asp).\n\n A record in MongoDB is a document, which is a data structure composed of key value pairs similar to the structure of JSON objects.\n\n Learn MongoDB now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_get_started.php)\n\n Become MongoDB Certified\n\n Get certified with our MongoDB exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-mongodb)\n\n Certified MongoDB Developer \n The candidate has passed the exam at the Professional level. \n Verify at \n verify.w3schools.com \n Stale Refsnes \n for w3schools.com \n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n A MongoDB Document\n\n Records in a MongoDB database are called documents, and the field values may include numbers, strings, booleans, arrays, or even nested documents.\n\n Example Document\n\n {\n title: \"Post Title 1\",\n body: \"Body of post.\",\n category: \"News\",\n likes: 1,\n tags: [\"news\", \"events\"],\n date: Date()\n}\n\n Learning by Examples\n\n Our \"Show MongoDB\" tool makes it easy to demonstrate MongoDB. It shows both the code and the result.\n\n Example\n\n Find all documents that have a category of \"news\".\n\n db.posts.find( {category: \"News\"} )\n \nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/showmongodb.php?filename=demo_find_query)\n\n Learning by Exercises\n\n MongoDB Exercises\n\n Exercise:\n\n What type of database is MongoDB?\n\nMongoDB is a database.\n\n Submit Answer &raquo; \n Start the Exercise (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/exercise.php?filename=exercise_get_started1)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/mongodb_get_started.php)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plan