in Inheritance (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_inheritance.php)\n\n Kotlin Cert\n\nKotlin Certificate (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_exam.php)\n\n Kotlin Examples\n\nKotlin Examples (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_examples.php)\nKotlin Compiler (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_compiler.php)\nKotlin Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_exercises.php)\nKotlin Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_quiz.php)\nKotlin Practice Problems (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_practice.php)\nKotlin Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_syllabus.php)\nKotlin Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_study_plan.php)\n\n Kotlin Tutorial \n\n ❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\n Next ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_intro.php)\n\n Learn Kotlin\n\n Kotlin is a modern, trending programming language.\n\n Kotlin is used to develop Android apps, server side apps, and much more.\n\n Learn Kotlin now ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_intro.php)\n\n Become Kotlin Certified\n\n Get certified with our Kotlin exam, includes a professionally curated study kit to guide you from beginner to exam-ready.\n\nGet Certified ❯ (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/course-catalog/products/learn-kotlin)\n\n Certified Kotlin Developer \n The candidate has passed the exam at the Professional level. \n Verify at \n verify.w3schools.com \n Stale Refsnes \n for w3schools.com \n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Examples in Each Chapter\n\n Our \"Try it Yourself\" editor makes it easy to learn Kotlin. You can edit the \ncode and view the result in your browser:\n\n Example\n\n fun main() {\n println(\"Hello World\")\n} \nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/trykotlin.php?filename=demo_helloworld)\n\n Click on the \"Try it Yourself\" button to see how it works. \n\n We recommend reading this tutorial, in the sequence listed in the left menu.\n\n Kotlin Exercises\n\n Test Yourself With Exercises\n\n Exercise:\n\n Insert the missing part of the code below to output \"Hello World\".\n\n () {\n println(\"Hello World\")\n}\n\n Submit Answer &raquo; \n Start the Exercise (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/exercise.php?filename=exercise_syntax1)\n\n Kotlin Quiz\n\n Learn by taking a quiz! This quiz will give you a signal of how much you know about Kotlin.\n\n Take the Kotlin Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_quiz.php)\n\n Learn by Examples\n\n Learn by examples! This tutorial supplements all explanations with clarifying examples.\n\n See All Kotlin Examples (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_examples.php)\n\n Download Kotlin\n\n Download Kotlin from github:\nhttps://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin (https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin)\n\n Track Your Progress\n\n Create a W3Schools account and get access to more features and learning materials:\n\n View your completed tutorials, exercises, and quizzes\n\n Keep an eye on your progress and daily streaks\n\n Join the leaderboard and compete with others\n\n Get your own avatar and unlock new skins\n\n Create your own personal website\n\n Sign Up &raquo; (https://profile.w3schools.com/sign-up)\n\n Note\n\n This is an optional feature. You can study at W3Schools without creating an account.\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/kotlin_intro.php)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n Learn more about Adventure Mode&rsaquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/adventure/)\n\n Free account\n\n Track your progress\n\n XP earned 0 \n Day streak 0 \n Spaces 0 \n League &mdash; \n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n New\n\n Le