ault.asp)\n PANDAS (https://www.w3schools.com/python/pandas/default.asp)\n NODEJS (https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/default.asp)\n DSA (https://www.w3schools.com/dsa/index.php)\n TYPESCRIPT (https://www.w3schools.com/typescript/index.php)\n ANGULAR (https://www.w3schools.com/angular/default.asp)\n ANGULARJS (https://www.w3schools.com/angularjs/default.asp)\n GIT (https://www.w3schools.com/git/default.asp)\n POSTGRESQL (https://www.w3schools.com/postgresql/index.php)\n MONGODB (https://www.w3schools.com/mongodb/index.php)\n ASP (https://www.w3schools.com/asp/default.asp)\n AI (https://www.w3schools.com/ai/default.asp)\n R (https://www.w3schools.com/r/default.asp)\n GO (https://www.w3schools.com/go/index.php)\n KOTLIN (https://www.w3schools.com/kotlin/index.php)\n SWIFT (https://www.w3schools.com/swift/default.asp)\n SASS (https://www.w3schools.com/sass/default.asp)\n VUE (https://www.w3schools.com/vue/index.php)\n GEN AI (https://www.w3schools.com/gen_ai/index.php)\n SCIPY (https://www.w3schools.com/python/scipy/index.php)\n CYBERSECURITY (https://www.w3schools.com/cybersecurity/index.php)\n DATA SCIENCE (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/default.asp)\n INTRO TO PROGRAMMING (https://www.w3schools.com/programming/index.php)\n INTRO TO HTML & CSS (https://www.w3schools.com/htmlcss/default.asp)\n BASH (https://www.w3schools.com/bash/index.php)\n RUST (https://www.w3schools.com/rust/index.php)\n TOOLS (https://www.w3schools.com/tools/index.php)\n\n Data Science \n\nDS HOME (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/default.asp)\nDS Introduction (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_introduction.asp)\nDS What is Data (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_data.asp)\nDS Database Table (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_database.asp)\nDS Python (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_python.asp)\nDS DataFrame (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_python_dataframe.asp)\nDS Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_functions.asp)\nDS Data Preparation (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_analyze_data.asp)\n\n DS Math \n\nDS Linear Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_functions.asp)\nDS Plotting Functions (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_functions_graphic.asp)\nDS Slope and Intercept (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_slope.asp)\n\n DS Statistics \n\nStat Introduction (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_intro.asp)\nStat Percentiles (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_percentiles.asp)\nStat Standard Deviation (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_std.asp)\nStat Variance (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_variance.asp)\nStat Correlation (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_correlation.asp)\nStat Correlation Matrix (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_correlation_matrix.asp)\nStat Correlation vs Causality (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_stat_correlation_causality.asp)\n\n DS Advanced \n\nDS Linear Regression (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression.asp)\nDS Regression Table (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_table.asp)\nDS Regression Info (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_info.asp)\nDS Regression Coefficients (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_coeff.asp)\nDS Regression P-Value (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_pvalue.asp)\nDS Regression R-Squared (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_rsquared.asp)\nDS Linear Regression Case (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_linear_regression_case.asp)\n\n DS Cert \n\nDS Certificate (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_exam.asp)\n\n Data Science Tutorial \n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_introduction.asp)\n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n Learn Data Science\n\n Today, Data rules the world. This has resulted in a huge demand for Data Scientists.\n\n A Data Scientist helps companies with data-driven decisions, to make their business better.\n\nStart learning Data Science now &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_introduction.asp)\n\n Learning by Examples\n\n With our \"Try it Yourself\" editor, you can edit Python code and view the result.\n\n Example\n\n import pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy \n import stats\n\nfull_health_data = pd.read_csv(\"data.csv\", header=0, sep=\",\")\n\nx = full_health_data[\"Average_Pulse\"]\ny = full_health_data[\"Calorie_Burnage\"]\n\nslope, intercept, r, p, std_err = stats.linregress(x, y)\n\ndef myfunc(x):\n return \n slope * x + intercept\n\nmymodel = list(map(myfunc, x))\n\nplt.scatter(x, y)\nplt.plot(x, mymodel)\nplt.ylim(ymin=0, ymax=2000)\n\n plt.xlim(xmin=0, xmax=200)\nplt.xlabel(\"Average_Pulse\")\nplt.ylabel (\"Calorie_Burnage\")\n\n plt.show()\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/trypython_multi_csv.asp?filename=demo_lr_least_square&multi=demo_data_full_multi)\n\n Click on the \"Try it Yourself\" button to see how it works. \n\n The Python Language\n\n Python is a programming language widely used by Data Scientists.\n\n Python has in-built mathematical libraries and functions, making it easier to calculate mathematical problems and to perform data analysis.\n\n In this tutorial, we will use Python to provide practical examples.\n\n To learn more about Python, please visit our Python Tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/python/default.asp).\n\n❮ Home (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/default.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/datascience/ds_introduction.asp)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n Learn more about Adventure Mode&rsaquo;