l_challenges_canvas.asp)\n\nHTML SVG (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_svg.asp)\n \n SVG (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_svg.asp)\n Code Challenge (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges_svg.asp)\n\n HTML Media\n\nHTML Media (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_media.asp)\nHTML Video (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_video.asp)\n \n Video (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_video.asp)\n Code Challenge (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges_video.asp)\n\nHTML Audio (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_audio.asp)\n \n Audio (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_audio.asp)\n Code Challenge (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges_audio.asp)\n\nHTML Plug-ins (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_object.asp)\nHTML YouTube (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_youtube.asp)\n\n Web APIs\n\nWeb APIs (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_api_whatis.asp)\nGeolocation API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_geolocation.asp)\nDrag and Drop API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_draganddrop.asp)\nPopover API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_popover.asp)\nWeb Storage API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_webstorage.asp)\nWeb Workers API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_webworkers.asp)\nServer-Sent Events API (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html5_serversentevents.asp)\n\n HTML Cert\n\nHTML Certificate (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_exam.asp)\n\n HTML Examples\n\nHTML Examples (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_examples.asp)\nHTML Editor (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_editor.asp)\nHTML Quiz (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_quiz.asp)\nHTML Exercises (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_exercises.asp)\nHTML Challenges (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges.asp)\nHTML Website (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_website.asp)\nHTML Syllabus (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_syllabus.asp)\nHTML Study Plan (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_study_plan.asp)\nHTML Interview Prep (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_interview_prep.asp)\nHTML Summary (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_summary.asp)\nHTML Accessibility (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_accessibility.asp)\n\n HTML References\n\nHTML Tag List (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/default.asp)\nHTML Attributes (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_attributes.asp)\nHTML Global Attributes (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_standardattributes.asp)\nHTML Browser Support (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_html_browsersupport.asp)\nHTML Events (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_eventattributes.asp)\nHTML Colors (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_colornames.asp)\nHTML Canvas (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_canvas.asp)\nHTML Audio/Video (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_av_dom.asp)\nHTML Doctypes (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_html_dtd.asp)\nHTML Character Sets (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_charactersets.asp)\nHTML URL Encode (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_urlencode.asp)\nHTML Lang Codes (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_language_codes.asp)\nHTTP Messages (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_httpmessages.asp)\nHTTP Methods (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_httpmethods.asp)\nPX to EM Converter (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_pxtoemconversion.asp)\nKeyboard Shortcuts (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/ref_keyboardshortcuts.asp)\n\n HTML Quotation and Citation Elements \n\n❮ Previous (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges_formatting.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_exercise_embed.asp?topic=quotation_elements)\n\n In this chapter we will go through the \n <blockquote> , <q> , <abbr> , <address> , <cite> , \nand <bdo> HTML elements.\n\n Example\n\n Here is a quote from WWF\'s website:\n\n For 60 years, WWF has worked to help people and nature thrive. As the world\'s \n leading conservation organization, WWF works in nearly 100 countries. At every \n level, we collaborate with people around the world to develop and deliver \n innovative solutions that protect communities, wildlife, and the places in \n which they live. \n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_intro2)\n\n Share \n\n Link Copied \n\n HTML <blockquote> for Quotations\n\n The HTML <blockquote> element defines a section that \nis quoted from another source.\n\n Browsers usually indent <blockquote> elements.\n\n Example\n\n <p>Here is a quote from WWF\'s website:</p>\n<blockquote cite=\"http://www.worldwildlife.org/who/index.html\">\n\n For 60 years, WWF has worked to help people and nature thrive. As the world\'s \n leading conservation organization, WWF works in nearly 100 countries. At every \n level, we collaborate with people around the world to develop and deliver \n innovative solutions that protect communities, wildlife, and the places in \n which they live.\n</blockquote>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_blockquote)\n\n HTML <q> for Short Quotations\n\n The HTML <q> tag defines a short quotation.\n\n Browsers normally insert quotation marks around the quotation.\n\n Example\n\n <p>WWF\'s goal is to: <q>Build a future where people live in harmony with \n nature.</q></p>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_q)\n\n HTML <abbr> for Abbreviations\n\n The HTML <abbr> tag defines an abbreviation or an acronym, like \"HTML\", \n\"CSS\", \"Mr.\", \n\"Dr.\", \"ASAP\", \"ATM\".\n\n Marking abbreviations can give useful information to browsers, translation \nsystems and search-engines.\n\n Tip: Use the global title attribute to \nshow the description for the \nabbreviation/acronym when you mouse over the element. \n\n Example\n\n <p>The <abbr title=\"World Health Organization\">WHO</abbr> was founded in \n 1948.</p>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_abbr)\n\n HTML <address> for Contact Information\n\n The HTML <address> tag defines the contact information for the author/owner of a document \nor an article.\n\n The contact information can be an email address, URL, physical address, phone \nnumber, social media handle, etc.\n\n The text in the <address> element usually renders in italic, \nand browsers will\nalways add a line break before and after the <address> element.\n\n Example\n\n <address>\nWritten by John Doe.<br> \nVisit us at:<br>\nExample.com<br>\n\n Box 564, Disneyland<br>\nUSA\n</address>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_address)\n\n HTML <cite> for Work Title\n\n The HTML <cite> tag defines the title of a \ncreative work (e.g. a book, a poem, a song, a movie, a painting, a sculpture, etc.).\n\n Note: A person\'s name is not the title of a work.\n\n The text in the <cite> element usually renders in italic .\n\n Example\n\n <p><cite>The Scream</cite> by Edvard Munch. Painted in 1893.</p>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_cite)\n\n HTML <bdo> for Bi-Directional Override\n\n BDO stands for Bi-Directional Override.\n\n The HTML <bdo> tag is used to override \nthe current text direction:\n\n Example\n\n <bdo dir=\"rtl\">This text will be written from right to left</bdo>\n\nTry it Yourself &raquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_formatting_bdo)\n\n HTML Quotation and Citation Elements\n\n Tag \n Description \n\n <abbr> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_abbr.asp) \n Defines an abbreviation or acronym \n\n <address> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_address.asp) \n Defines contact information for the author/owner of a document \n\n <bdo> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_bdo.asp) \n Defines the text direction \n\n <blockquote> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_blockquote.asp) \n Defines a section that is quoted from another source \n\n <cite> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_cite.asp) \n Defines the title of a work \n\n <q> (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_q.asp) \n Defines a short inline quotation \n\n For a complete list of all available HTML tags, visit our HTML Tag Reference (https://www.w3schools.com/tags/default.asp).\n\n❮ Previous (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_challenges_formatting.asp)\nNext ❯ (https://www.w3schools.com/html/html_exercise_embed.asp?topic=quotation_elements)\n\n ★\n\n +1 (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fpathfinder.w3schools.com)\n\n REMOVE ADS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n Learn more about Adventure Mode&rsaquo; (https://www.w3schools.com/adventure/)\n\n Free account\n\n Track your progress\n\n XP earned 0 \n Day streak 0 \n Spaces 0 \n League &mdash; \n\n Sign in to track progress (https://profile.w3schools.com/log-in?redirect_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmy-learning.w3schools.com)\n\n New\n\n Learn in Adventure Mode \n W3Schools Adventure App \n\n Coding fundamentals as bite-sized lessons and challenges.\n\n PLUS (https://order.w3schools.com/plans)\n\n SPACES (https://www.w3schools.com/spaces/index.php)\n\n GET CERTIFIED (https://campus.w3schools.com/collections/certifications)\n\n FOR TEACHERS (https://www.w3schools.com/academy/index.php)\n\n PRACTICE (https://www.w3schools.com/practice/index.php)\n\n CONTACT US\n\n &times; \n Contact Sales\n\n If you want to use W3Schools services as an educational institution, team or enterprise, send us an e-mail:\nsales@w3schools.com\n\n Report Error\n\n If you want to report an error, or if you want to make a suggestion, send us an e-mail:\nhelp@w3schools.com\n\n Top Tutorials\n\n HTML Tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/html/default.asp)\n\n CSS Tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/css/default.asp)\n\n JavaScript Tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/js/default.asp)\n\n How To Tutorial (https://www.w3schools.com/howto/default.asp)\n\n SQL Tutorial (https://www.w