elopment\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about using the canvas element or handling images in web development?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216c0616dd2a31052582acb1d584b9d737be00c513acb\"}','2026-10-05 05:48:35'),(1097,16,7,36,'USER','Canvas element','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216c0616dd2a31052582acb1d584b9d737be00c513acb\"}','2026-10-05 05:48:49'),(1098,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','The <canvas> element is used to draw graphics via scripting. By default, it features a coordinate space or grid where 1 unit corresponds to 1 pixel, with the origin (0,0) positioned in the top-left corner. To display anything on a canvas, a script must first access its rendering context using the getContext() method. For 2D graphics, you specify \"2d\" to obtain a CanvasRenderingContext2D. Additionally, canvas content is not part of the DOM and is not accessible to screen readers by default, so descriptive fallback content, aria-label, or role=\"presentation\" should be used when appropriate.\n\nWould you like to know more about drawing rectangles, drawing paths, or applying styles and colors on the canvas?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"The <canvas> element is used to draw graphics via scripting. By default, it features a coordinate space or grid where 1 unit corresponds to 1 pixel, with the origin (0,0) positioned in the top-left corner. To display anything on a canvas, a script must first access its rendering context using the getContext() method. For 2D graphics, you specify \\\"2d\\\" to obtain a CanvasRenderingContext2D. Additionally, canvas content is not part of the DOM and is not accessible to screen readers by default, so descriptive fallback content, aria-label, or role=\\\"presentation\\\" should be used when appropriate.\", \"suggestions\": [\"Drawing rectangles\", \"Drawing paths\", \"Applying styles and colors\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about drawing rectangles, drawing paths, or applying styles and colors on the canvas?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216c0616dd2a31052582acb1d584b9d737be00c513acb\"}','2026-10-05 05:48:51'),(1099,81,7,80,'USER','What is Django and what is it used for?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"0b93c0945908d4731447acfd81ebca20066707929a6f425087cb7a2518d288b3\"}','2026-10-05 05:54:12'),(1100,81,7,80,'ASSISTANT','Django is a high-level Python web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design. It is used to build better web apps more quickly and with less code, helping developers take applications from concept to completion while handling much of the hassle of web development.\n\nWould you like to learn more about how to get started with Django or explore its key features?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"Django is a high-level Python web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design. It is used to build better web apps more quickly and with less code, helping developers take applications from concept to completion while handling much of the hassle of web development.\", \"suggestions\": [\"How do I get started with Django?\", \"What makes Django secure and scalable?\", \"Where can I learn more about About Django?\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about how to get started with Django or explore its key features?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"0b93c0945908d4731447acfd81ebca20066707929a6f425087cb7a2518d288b3\"}','2026-10-05 05:54:13'),(1101,81,7,80,'USER','How do I get started with Django?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"0b93c0945908d4731447acfd81ebca20066707929a6f425087cb7a2518d288b3\"}','2026-10-05 05:54:13'),(1102,81,7,80,'ASSISTANT','To get involved with Django, you can join a group, contribute to Django, submit a bug, or report a security issue. You can also get help by checking the Getting Help FAQ, joining the Django Discord, or visiting the Official Django Forum.\n\nWould you like to know how to join a group or visit the official Django for