on-type(...).\", \"suggestions\": [\"Animating Suspense Fallbacks\", \"Transition Types in CSS\", \"React 19.3 Features\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about animating Suspense fallbacks or using transition types with View Transitions?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:09'),(1198,16,7,36,'USER','React 19.3 Features','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:17'),(1199,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React 19.3 introduces several new stable features, including View Transitions, Fragment Refs, browser support, and Trusted Types support. Additionally, it allows <Context> to be rendered directly in Server Components.\n\nWould you like to know more about Fragment Refs or Trusted Types support in React 19.3?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React 19.3 introduces several new stable features, including View Transitions, Fragment Refs, browser support, and Trusted Types support. Additionally, it allows <Context> to be rendered directly in Server Components.\", \"suggestions\": [\"Fragment Refs\", \"Trusted Types\", \"Server Components\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about Fragment Refs or Trusted Types support in React 19.3?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:21'),(1200,16,7,36,'USER','what is useState','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:31'),(1201,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','useState is a built-in Hook provided by React that lets you add state to a component. It takes the initial state and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it.\n\nWould you like to know more about declaring state variables or using other built-in Hooks?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"useState is a built-in Hook provided by React that lets you add state to a component. It takes the initial state and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it.\", \"suggestions\": [\"State Variables\", \"State Setter Function\", \"Built-in Hooks\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about declaring state variables or using other built-in Hooks?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:32'),(1202,16,7,36,'USER','State Variables','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:38'),(1203,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','Unlike regular JavaScript variables, React state behaves more like a snapshot. Setting state does not change the existing state variable immediately, but instead triggers a re-render to update the UI.\n\nWould you like to learn how to structure your state well or how to share state between components?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"Unlike regular JavaScript variables, React state behaves more like a snapshot. Setting state does not change the existing state variable immediately, but instead triggers a re-render to update the UI.\", \"suggestions\": [\"State as a Snapshot\", \"Choosing State Structure\", \"Sharing State\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn how to structure your state well or how to share state between components?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:41'),(1204,16,7,36,'USER','Sharing State','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 06:15:50'),(1205,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','You can share state between components by lifting state up to keep components in sync.\n\nWould you like to learn more about preserving and resetting state or extracting state logic into a reducer?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"You can share s