components (such as buttons), you can ensure that they all share and update together based on the same state variable.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184527780-4d07cbbf\", \"suggestions\": [\"Managing State\", \"Sharing State Between Components\", \"Quick Start\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about managing state or sharing state between components?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:27'),(1470,93,7,36,'USER','What are React components?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:27'),(1471,16,7,36,'USER','what  is the full form of csss','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:28'),(1472,93,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React uses trees to model the relationships between components and modules, where a React render tree represents the parent and child relationships between components. Components near the top of the tree, near the root component, are top-level components, while components with no child components are leaf components. Additionally, built-in components are available for use in JSX, and you can define custom wrapper components or use features like React Server Components.\n\nWould you like to learn more about top-level components, leaf components, or React Server Components?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React uses trees to model the relationships between components and modules, where a React render tree represents the parent and child relationships between components. Components near the top of the tree, near the root component, are top-level components, while components with no child components are leaf components. Additionally, built-in components are available for use in JSX, and you can define custom wrapper components or use features like React Server Components.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184529259-64de6bc4\", \"suggestions\": [\"Top-level components\", \"Leaf components\", \"React Server Components\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about top-level components, leaf components, or React Server Components?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:29'),(1473,93,7,36,'USER','What is useState?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:29'),(1474,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','I could not find the full form of \"csss\" in the available website excerpts. Would you like to connect with a support team member or representative for further assistance?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"I could not find the full form of \\\"csss\\\" in the available website excerpts. Would you like to connect with a support team member or representative for further assistance?\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184529978-9dce41ac\", \"suggestions\": [\"What is React?\", \"What are React Versions?\", \"What is Quick Start?\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:29'),(1475,93,7,36,'ASSISTANT','The useState Hook is a built-in Hook provided by React that lets you declare a state variable in a component. It takes an initial state as an argument and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it. When you call the setter function with a new value, React updates the state and triggers a re-render of the component.\n\nWould you like to know more about how to use useState, custom Hooks, or other built-in Hooks?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"The useState Hook is a built-in Hook provided by React that lets you declare a state variable in a component. It takes an initial state as an argument and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it. When you call the setter function with a new value, React updates the state and triggers a re-render of the component.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184530715-187c4742\", \"suggestions\": [\"Using Hooks\", \"Custom Hooks\", \"Built-in Hooks\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about how to use useState, custom Hooks, or other built-in Hooks?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:30'),(1476,93,7,36,'USER','What is useState and useEffect?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:15:30'),(1477,93,7,36,'ASSISTANT','The useState Hook is a built-in function that lets you declare a state variable in a component, taking an initial state and returning the current state alongside a state setter function to update it. The useEffect Hook is used to synchronize components with external systems, manage video playback based on props, or set up connections like a chat server, and many Effects can also return a cleanup function to disconnect or clean up after themselves.\n\nWould you like to know more about how to use useState, cleanup functions, or synchronizing with Effects?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"The useState Hook is a built-in function that lets you declare a state variable in a component, taking an initial state and returning the current state alongside a state setter function to update it. The useEffect Hook is used to synchronize components with external systems, manage video playback based on props, or set up connections like a chat server, and many Effects can also return a cleanup function to disconnect or clean up after themselves.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184532385-21296587\", \"suggestions\": [\"useState Hook\", \"useEffect Hook\", \"Cleanup Functions\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about how to use useState, cleanup functions, or synchronizing with Effects?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e666