e down from a parent component to its children by using JSX curly braces as props (for example, passing state values and event handlers down to child components like <MyButton count={count} onClick={handleClick} />).\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184574771-3e538433\", \"suggestions\": [\"Managing State\", \"Passing Data Deeply\", \"Extracting State Logic\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about moving state up or passing data deeply without prop drilling?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:16:14'),(1490,16,7,36,'USER','what is the state','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:16:33'),(1491,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','In React, state allows components to remember information, such as user input or data that changes over time, instead of modifying the UI directly. By using state variables (declared via the useState Hook), you can describe the UI for different visual states of your component and trigger updates in response to user interaction.\n\nWould you like to learn how to declare a state variable or how components render and commit state changes?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"In React, state allows components to remember information, such as user input or data that changes over time, instead of modifying the UI directly. By using state variables (declared via the useState Hook), you can describe the UI for different visual states of your component and trigger updates in response to user interaction.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184595397-551d9f87\", \"suggestions\": [\"State: A Component\'s Memory\", \"Rendering and Committing\", \"Managing State\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn how to declare a state variable or how components render and commit state changes?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:16:35'),(1492,16,7,36,'USER','what is react js','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:16:54'),(1493,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React features components, hooks, APIs, and directives for building user interfaces. It includes React DOM features for web applications running in the browser DOM environment, as well as the React Compiler, which is a build-time optimization tool that automatically memoizes React components and values.\n\nWould you like to explore React Hooks, components, or the React Compiler configuration options?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React features components, hooks, APIs, and directives for building user interfaces. It includes React DOM features for web applications running in the browser DOM environment, as well as the React Compiler, which is a build-time optimization tool that automatically memoizes React components and values.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184616254-1a0590d3\", \"suggestions\": [\"React Hooks\", \"React Components\", \"React Compiler\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to explore React Hooks, components, or the React Compiler configuration options?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:16:56'),(1494,94,7,36,'USER','What is the price of idli?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:09'),(1495,94,7,36,'ASSISTANT','I could not find information about the price of idli in the currently indexed website content, as the available website excerpts only contain documentation related to React.\n\nWould you like to explore topics available on this website, such as React, React Versions, Quick Start?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"I could not find information about the price of idli in the currently indexed website content, as the available website excerpts only contain documentation related to React.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184631654-207eb70c\", \"suggestions\": [\"What is React?\", \"What are React Versions?\", \"What is Quick Start?\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to explore topics available on this website, such as React, React Versions, Quick Start?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:11'),(1496,94,7,36,'USER','What is lifting state up in React?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:11'),(1497,94,7,36,'ASSISTANT','Lifting state up is a technique in React where you move state up to a parent component in order to share it between multiple child components. By passing the new state value and an event handler as props to each child component, they can all display and update together based on that shared state.\n\nWould you like to learn more about sharing state between components or managing state in React?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"Lifting state up is a technique in React where you move state up to a parent component in order to share it between multiple child components. By passing the new state value and an event handler as props to each child component, they can all display and update together based on that shared state.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184633372-cc7fac95\", \"suggestions\": [\"Sharing State Between Components\", \"Managing State\", \"Adding Interactivity\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about sharing state between components or managing state in React?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:13'),(1498,94,7,36,'USER','What are React components?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:13'),(1499,94,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React components are modeled using trees to represent parent and child relationships. Components near the root are considered top-level components, while components with no child components are leaf components. Additionally, React provides built-in components that you can use in your JSX, and Server Components that allow you to render features like Context directly.\n\nWould you like to learn more about React render trees or explore Server Components?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React components are modeled using trees to represent parent and child relationships. Components near the root are considered top-level components, while components with no child components are leaf components. Additionally, React provides built-in components that you can use in your JSX, and Server Components that allow you to render features like Context directly.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184634612-53216c46\", \"suggestions\": [\"React Render Trees\", \"Server Components\", \"React Reference Overview\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about React render trees or explore Server Components?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:14'),(1500,94,7,36,'USER','What is useState?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:14'),(1501,94,7,36,'ASSISTANT','The useState Hook is a built-in function provided by React that lets you add state to a component. It takes an initial state as an argument and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it. When you call the setter function with a new value, React updates the state and re-renders the component.\n\nWould you like to learn more about how state updates trigger re-renders or explore other built-in React Hooks?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"The useState Hook is a built-in function provided by React that lets you add state to a component. It takes an initial state as an argument and returns a pair of values: the current state and a state setter function that lets you update it. When you call the setter function with a new value, React updates the state and re-renders the component.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184636252-987f871e\", \"suggestions\": [\"Using Hooks\", \"Adding Interactivity\", \"Quick Start\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about how state updates trigger re-renders or explore other built-in React Hooks?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:16'),(1502,94,7,36,'USER','What is useState and useEffect?','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:17:16'),(1503,94,7,36,'ASSISTANT','The useState Hook is a built-in function that lets you declare a state variable, taking an initial state and returning the current state along with a state setter function to update it. The useEffect Hook is used to synchronize components with external systems, such as setting up connections or interacting with browser elements like a video player, and many Effects can also return a cleanup function to clean up after themselves.\n\nWould you like to learn more about how to synchronize components with external systems using Effects?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"The useState Hook is a built-in function that lets you declare a state variable, taking an initial state and returning the current state along with a state setter function to update it. The useEffect Hook is used to synchronize components with external systems, such as setting up connections or interacting with browser elements like a video player, and many Effects can also return a cleanup function to clean up after themselves.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184637773-f4884a65\", \"suggestions\": [\"useState Hook\", \"useEffect Hook\", \"Synchronizing with Effects\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about how to synchronize components with external systems using Effects?\", \"s