2026-10-05 07:18:19'),(1512,16,7,36,'USER','what is props','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:18:30'),(1513,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React components use props to communicate with each other. Every parent component can pass information to its child components by giving them props. Props are similar to HTML attributes, and you can pass any JavaScript value through them, including objects, arrays, functions, and JSX.\n\nWould you like to learn more about passing props to a component or lifting state up?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React components use props to communicate with each other. Every parent component can pass information to its child components by giving them props. Props are similar to HTML attributes, and you can pass any JavaScript value through them, including objects, arrays, functions, and JSX.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184712414-78e7f495\", \"suggestions\": [\"Passing Props\", \"Lifting State Up\", \"Parent and Child Components\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about passing props to a component or lifting state up?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:18:32'),(1514,16,7,36,'USER','tell me about props and props drilling','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:22:08'),(1515,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','React components use props to communicate with each other, allowing parent components to pass information (such as objects, arrays, functions, and JSX) down to their child components. Regarding prop drilling, the available website excerpts mention how to pass information without prop drilling using context, but do not provide detailed definitions or instructions on prop drilling itself.\n\nWould you like to learn more about how to pass information deeply with context or read about passing props to a component?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"React components use props to communicate with each other, allowing parent components to pass information (such as objects, arrays, functions, and JSX) down to their child components. Regarding prop drilling, the available website excerpts mention how to pass information without prop drilling using context, but do not provide detailed definitions or instructions on prop drilling itself.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791184931155-159c5749\", \"suggestions\": [\"Passing Data with Context\", \"Passing Props to a Component\", \"Managing State\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to learn more about how to pass information deeply with context or read about passing props to a component?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:22:11'),(1516,16,7,36,'USER','Passing Data with Context','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"3dc86e6666d7a5f236ea594bf10bb95726c2fa7538d7e755dc766aa1561e2feb\"}','2026-10-05 07:22:26'),(1517,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','Usually, you will pass information from a parent component to a child component via props. However, passing props can become inconvenient if you need to pass some prop through many components or if many components need the same information. Context lets a parent component make information available to any component in the tree below it—no matter how deep it is—without passing it explicitly through props.\n\nWould you like to learn more about passing data deeply with context or scaling up with reducer and context?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"Usually, you will pass information from a parent component to a child component via props. However, passing props can become inconvenient if you need to pass some prop through many components or if many components need the same information. Context lets a parent component make information available to any component in the tree below it—no matter how deep it is—without passing it explicitly through props.\", \"turn_