int\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216c0616dd2a31052582acb1d584b9d737be00c513acb\"}','2026-10-05 07:38:32'),(1573,16,7,36,'ASSISTANT','I found information regarding the differences between tasks and microtasks in JavaScript, but your question appears to be incomplete. Based on the available excerpts, tasks and microtasks are both made up of JavaScript code placed on a queue and run at an appropriate time, but the event loop handles them differently: the microtask queue is processed multiple times per iteration of the event loop (each time a task exits and returns control, or after handling events), and any new microtasks added via queueMicrotask() execute immediately until the microtask queue is completely empty before the next task runs.\n\nWould you like to know more about how to use microtasks or how tasks and microtasks differ in the event loop?','SENT','{\"answer\": \"I found information regarding the differences between tasks and microtasks in JavaScript, but your question appears to be incomplete. Based on the available excerpts, tasks and microtasks are both made up of JavaScript code placed on a queue and run at an appropriate time, but the event loop handles them differently: the microtask queue is processed multiple times per iteration of the event loop (each time a task exits and returns control, or after handling events), and any new microtasks added via queueMicrotask() execute immediately until the microtask queue is completely empty before the next task runs.\", \"turn_id\": \"turn-1791185914014-5d9b1773\", \"suggestions\": [\"Microtasks and Tasks\", \"Using queueMicrotask\", \"Event Loop\"], \"follow_up_prompt\": \"Would you like to know more about how to use microtasks or how tasks and microtasks differ in the event loop?\", \"source_fingerprint\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216c0616dd2a31052582acb1d584b9d737be00c513acb\"}','2026-10-05 07:38:34'),(1574,16,7,36,'USER','tell me what is the state and crops','SENT','{\"source_fingerprint\": \"adaafd8d683312381e0216